FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/interpreter.rs:1289-1299 — Prefix collision in `module_member_values`: The function uses `strip_prefix("{module}_")` to extract member names from qualified members (e.g., `MathUtils_circle_area` → `circle_area`). This incorrectly matches qualified members from other modules whose names share the same prefix — e.g., if modules `foo` and `fooBar` both exist, `fooBar_baz` would be misattributed to module `foo` as member `Bar_baz`. This causes wrong member listings in `.env` for prefix-overlapping module names. VERIFIED: Code trace shows line 1291 extracts `member = qualified.strip_prefix(&prefix)` without verifying the prefix corresponds to an exact module boundary.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:890-893 — Unbounded recursion in `collect_shape_labels`: The function recursively walks `Value::List` elements without a depth limit. A program can create arbitrarily deep nesting at runtime (e.g., `repeat 10000 times set x to [x] end` within the 1M iteration limit), causing stack overflow when `.types` is invoked. The REPORT.md claims this is not an issue because "Redblue values are acyclic", but acyclic does not imply bounded depth. VERIFIED: Code at lines 890-893 recurses on each list item with no depth counter or bound.
3. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2876-2883 — Variable shadowing by imports in `.env`: `environment_lines` filters session bindings whose names match any imported module's bound name (line 2883). If a user variable shares a name with an import bound name (e.g., `set files to "x"` then `import files`), the variable is hidden from the session section. The comment at line 2872-2874 documents this as intentional, but it is a usability hazard with no test covering the shadowing case.
4. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:12471-12501 — Missing test for constants in imported modules: Test `environment_has_session_import_and_builtin_sections` only asserts function members (`MathUtils.circle_area`) appear in `.env` imports section. Constants (`PI`, `TAU` in `MathUtils`) are valid module members but are not verified to appear. The test at line 6882 checks `TAU` reaches session names but not the `.env` imports listing.
5. [STYLE] src/interpreter.rs:1253-1254 — Redundant `dedup()` in `imported_modules`: The function collects from `module_aliases` (a `HashMap<bound, module>`), sorts by bound name, then calls `dedup()`. Since each bound name is unique in the map, no duplicates can exist; `dedup()` is a no-op.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
